            "mimeType": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
            "text": "[{\"id\":\"01cef75e-7200-4369-92ef-69d4a7b437c2\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: World Horror Shorts - SHORTS 5\",\"description\":\"30th October 5pm £12\\n\\na selection of fantastic short horror films from across the world.\\n\\nExuvia\\t(Arthur Henning\\tAustria)\\nDon't go \\t(Talon Darren Winsnes\\tNorway)\\nIn case of fear\\t(Aaron Sauerland\\tUS)\\nScroll\\t(Utku Banci\\tCanada)\\nFavela Amarela\\t(Nícolas Lobato, Thiago Tuchu\\tBrazil)\\nThe Binding\\t(Ryan Kennedy\\tUS)\\nGumboro\\t(Dimitris Vavatsis\\tGreece)\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790763067284_4EpIAAvwb.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T10:11:09.325964+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-13T11:07:48.8248+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abce03cead997d09a6b291b\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-world-horror-shorts\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"834ee49d-9e43-4935-85d7-a9772e334bde\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Film Festival 2026: Day 6 (Hen & Chickens Theatre)\",\"description\":\"2nd May 11.30am £12\\n\\nOllie, a hopeless romantic scarred by a string of unfaithful partners, finally finds 'the one'. But when he grows suspicious that his fiancée might also be cheating, his struggle to protect love spirals into a comedic and chaotic battle with his own insecurities.\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/tickets.okedia.com/event_cover/screenshot-2026-03-22-at-002914-y73Yk.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-04-06T10:09:37.58121+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-06T12:48:24.915653+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":null,\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"169\",\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-film-festival-2026-day-6-hen-chickens-theatre\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"046f5082-ab19-45bf-83b0-05874985ee3b\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Film Festival 2026: Day 2 (Odeon Luxe & Dine Islington))\",\"description\":\"28th April 6 pm £12\\n\\nShort selections from UK Filmmakers\\n\\nScreen 1 - 6 pm\\nCarrot Cake(Olive Pascha)\\nWhere There's Light (Charlotte Couture)\\nBeauty Sleep (Jasmine Emma De Silva)\\nThe Black Box: Awaken (Rebecca Holbourn)\\nGrandma is Thirsty (Kris Carr)\\nStumbling Blocks (Tortor Smith)\\nPlastic Surgery (Guy Trevellyan)\\nToad in the Hole (Ben Norris)\\n\\nScreen 5 - **6pm**\\nI Am the Prize (Sai Karan Talwar)\\nEvery Time I See a Yellow Car (Matt Chandler)\\nVEGETABLES HAVE SUGAR (Daniel Liakh)\\nKen (Alison Hargreaves)\\nIn the Clouds (Alexandra Bahíyyih Wain)\\nHomonym (Lily Howkins)\\nLost Dog (Simon Wade, Paul Wade)\\nDating Mark Silcox (Joe Lycett)\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/tickets.okedia.com/event_cover/screenshot-2026-03-21-at-173308-L5mcC.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-04-06T10:09:37.389781+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-14T08:06:41.301675+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":null,\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"797893a8-e6f4-4f29-a91e-2dd6f187ad77\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"166\",\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-film-festival-2026-day-2-odeon-luxe-dine-islington\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"72f1adba-5df1-4e9d-be6e-f6a1c937c0d7\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Film Festival 2026: Day 7 (Genesis Cinema, Whitechapel)\",\"description\":\"3rd May £12 \\n\\n\\n\\n12.45pm - UK Shorts 6\\n\\nThe Painting & The Statue (Freddie Fox)\\n\\nThe Weight of Feeling (Lily Mellor)\\n\\nThe Weight (Vanessa Rose)\\n\\nStarboy (AR Ugas)\\n\\nRoute Cause (Eliab Gebressilase)\\n\\nOvertones (Ollie Gardner)\\n\\nA Wonderful Neighbour (Alun Rhys Morgan)\\n\\nDomestic (Jake Spence Barnes)\\n\\nEmiko Jones (Hanako Footman)\\n\\n________________________________\\n\\n4.30pm - 8pm £12\\n\\nTHE UNRESTRICTED VIEW FILM FESTIVAL AWARDS 2026\\n\\nA drinks reception followed by an awards event\",\"price\":0.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1775581095986_V9aiuLJ0S.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-04-07T16:58:18.296694+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-07T16:58:18.296694+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"69d537a95c7cd75eb8c57eba\",\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"ce050077-3921-405b-8b52-8a21a9030135\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"172\",\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-film-festival-2026-day-7-genesis-cinema-whitechapel\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"2a7e44fa-14ff-4f2f-8008-514c695c3f9b\",\"title\":\"London Fetish Film Festival: INSIDE FETISH EXCLUSIVE SCREENING\",\"description\":\"INSIDE FETISH EXCLUSIVE SCREENING\\n\\nSaturday June 6th 7pm £12\\n\\nRun Time: 70mins + Panel Q&A\\n\\nJoin the London Fetish Film Festival for an exclusive pop-up screening exploring BDSM, kink, fetish, and body-based performance through experimental cinema and documentary film.\\n\\nTaking place on Saturday 6th June, this curated programme features short films by international artists including Peter Cage, Finn Darrel, Odette Engle, Rebecca Rütten, and Jamie Butine, offering perspectives on private sessions, fetish practices, intimacy, identity, and embodied performance.\\n\\nThe screening will be followed by a live panel discussion and open Q&A with special guests, and further announcements to follow…\\n\\nTHE PROGRAMME (in no particular order):\\n\\nON THE EROTICS OF STUFFING LARGE OBJECTS INTO SMALL SPACES\\nBy Peter Cage\\n15mins\\n\\nAn experimental film exploring the submissive desire for restrictive bondage. A solitary figure, hooded and confined within a dog crate, shares an intimate internal monologue: “This cage will never be comfortable, though I find it deeply comforting.”\\n\\nBREAKFAST TIME\\nBy Peter Cage\\n17mins 58secs\\n\\nA raw and intimate documentary following a queer pup eating breakfast from his dog bowl. Through candid voiceover, the film unfolds reflections on desire, disgust, failed relationships, experiences of homophobic violence, and the isolation attached to stigmatised desire.\\n\\nBABY BLUE\\nBy Finn Darrel\\n4mins 27secs\\n\\nAn exploration of tenderness and catharsis through needle play. Filmed on Finn Darrel’s final day in New York City, the performance becomes both a goodbye and a rite of passage marking their return home.\\n\\nTHE ARCHITECT\\nBy Odette Engle\\n4mins 39secs\\n\\nPerformance artist Odette Engle undertakes a process of inverted architectural mapping upon the suspended body of Cute But Deadly.\\n\\nINSIGHT KINK\\nBy Rebecca Rütten, Phantessa and Mistress Deva\\n11mins 49secs\\nA collaborative exploration of kink, power exchange, and embodied performance through the perspectives of artists and practitioners working within BDSM culture.\\nDEEP IN\\nBy Jamie Butine\\n17mins 26secs\\n\\nWhat is pain to you? How deeply can you enter it? Deep In presents needle play as a ritual of emotional release, examining the relationship between physical pain, grief, sorrow, and catharsis.\\n\\n\\nABOUT LFFF:\\nLondon Fetish Film Festival is an international platform unleashing fearless cinema that dives into kink, fetish, BDSM, psychology, desire and power with hardcore substance, and zero shame. From arthouse to explicit, tender to transgressive, we celebrate films that smash taboos, challenge censorship, and electrify audiences through bold, provocative, and deeply human explorations of fetish culture and lifestyle.\\n\\nWe are currently accepting film submissions for LFFF 2027 here: London Fetish Film Festival - FilmFreeway \\n\\nFor the latest updates and information: https://www.instagram.com/londonfetishfilmfestival_\\n\",\"price\":0.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1779975969402_QFGxtjiJB.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-05-28T13:46:12.033807+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-05-28T13:48:58.726182+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6a1847235c7cd75eb8221042\",\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"208\",\"slug\":\"inside-fetish-exclusive-screening\",\"on_sale_date\":\"2026-05-27T23:00:00+00:00\",\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"3bffaa03-d98d-43be-8eed-9f9205f92027\",\"title\":\"UVHFF x About Bloody Time\",\"description\":\"31st October 4pm - 6pm £12.00\\n\\nA HALLOWEEN CELEBRATION OF WOMEN WORKING IN GENRE\\n\\n31 October 2026 | 4–6pm | Hen & Chickens Theatre, Islington\\n\\nThis Halloween, Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival is partnering with About Bloody Time, created by Yes She Cannes, for a special afternoon celebrating women shaping, creating and championing genre.\\n\\nMeet brilliant women and their work, swap your genre raves, rants & recommendations, discover opportunities worth sinking your teeth into and have a bloody good time.\\n\\nThis edition will spotlight She Builds Stories, an organisation helping women take their stories from idea to industry through creative development and tangible routes forward.\\n\\nTheir latest opportunity is the Female Vertical Drama Programme, in partnership with CenterFrame- inviting women to take a fresh look at vertical drama: why it matters for women, why horror fits the format, and the real opportunity women have to help shape what comes next.\\n\\nThe programme will select six female writers for a one-week development room in London, with one project ultimately produced as a pilot. Submissions are free and open until 14 November 2026. CenterFrame\\n\\nAlongside the spotlight, expect the full About Bloody Time atmosphere: celebrating bloody brilliant women working across genre, a few fun surprises built and plenty of space to meet new fellow filmmakers!\\n\\nAnd because it’s Halloween, Bloody/Halloween outfits are very much encouraged, with a prize for Best Bloody Fit!\\n\\nTogether we’re creating more spaces for women in genre. Coz it’s about bloody time. 🩸🕰️\\n\\nFind out more\\n\\nUnrestricted View Horror Film Festival — https://uvff.co.uk/uvhff-2026 | Instagram @uviewff\\n\\nAbout Bloody Time / Yes She Cannes — https://www.yesshecannes.com/ | Instagram @yeshecannes\\n\\nShe Builds Stories — https://shebuildsstories.com/  | Instagram @shebuildsstories\\n\\nCenterFrame — https://centerframe.club/ | Instagram @centerframeclub\\n\\nFemale Vertical Drama Programme / submissions  (https://centerframe.club/pages/shebuildsstories-female-vertical-drama-programme) — Programme details & apply\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1791802574216_jel6jmGoW.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-10-12T10:56:16.317104+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-12T10:56:16.317104+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6accbccfead997d09a0d6909\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"uvhff-x-about-bloody-time\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"11478474-5332-447c-93bb-22a7e96a9b34\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted Brew (Coffee, tea and industry talks.)\",\"description\":\"31st October 12pm - 3.30pm £12\\n\\n12pm - Coffee, tea & chats.\\n1pm - 30 minutes chat with Christian Parton from Genera about funding & their new distribution platform Hosted by Felicity Wren (VP of The International Screenwriters association)\\n1.30pm - Coffee, tea & chats.\\n2pm - TBC\\n2.30pm - Coffee, tea & chats.\\n3pm - 30 minutes chat with Christine Hartland from My Smash Media about building the right pitch and connecting creatives with industry professionals looking for their next project. Hosted by Felicity Wren (VP of The International Screenwriters association)\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1791804712400_trdaWbX1N.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-10-12T11:31:54.955557+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-12T11:32:15.934861+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6accc52aead997d09a334a8e\",\"age_rating\":\"16+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-brew-coffee-tea-and-industry-talks\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"c680d23e-fbb2-478b-a287-3839da280022\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Film Festival 2026: Day 6 (Curzon Hoxton)\",\"description\":\"2nd May 3.30pm & 6.30pm £12 each screening, both Screenings £18.\\n\\nSelections of UK short films.\\n\\n3.30 pm - UK shorts 4\\n\\nUncle Artoo(Zoe Whittaker)\\nIndignitas (Darcia Martin)\\nBetween the Piers (Kate Cheeseman)\\nCare(Stef O'Driscoll)\\nRule, Britannia (Max Fisher)\\nTruckload (Aella Jordon-Edge)\\nSelf+Tape(James Cleave)\\n\\n___________________________________\\n\\n6.30 pm - UK shorts 5\\n\\nMagid/Zafar(Luis Hindman)\\nBlackpool (Stephen Gallacher)\\nThe Humbug (Cole Paviour)\\nBig Breakfast (Chris Hyde)\\nGood Behaviour (Dan Sloan)\\nLargo (Salvatore Scarpa & Max Burgoyne-Moore)\\nGone for Milk (Will Ferrell)\\nEasy Sell (Ken Abalos & Ash Meshkati)\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/tickets.okedia.com/event_cover/screenshot-2026-03-22-at-150237-0ocKC.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-04-06T10:09:37.621633+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-06T12:50:56.534845+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":null,\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"2678eab5-e621-40dc-a29d-26c1ee4dbbe0\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"171\",\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-film-festival-2026-day-6-curzon-hoxton\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"629d8c1f-1dd7-4e7f-9784-36f8ffff9d6e\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Film Festival 2026: Full Festival Pass\",\"description\":\"28th April - 3rd May £40\\n\\nA pass for all screenings and events at the festival.\\n\\n(Everyman screenings need confirmation)\",\"price\":40.00,\"image_url\":\"https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/tickets.okedia.com/event_cover/screenshot-2026-03-21-at-105108-tnqFC.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-04-06T10:09:37.258477+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-06T12:37:42.889189+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":null,\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"173\",\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-film-festival-2026-full-festival-pass\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"76bb4c55-2145-4917-9341-088d20f80d8c\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Film Festival 2026: Day 4 (Hen & Chickens Theatre)\",\"description\":\"30th April £10-12 per screening, £18 for a day pass\\n\\n2pm - Feature\\n\\nTitle: The Legend of Juan Jose Mundo\\n\\nDirector: Michael Walker\\n\\nVenue: The Hen & Chickens Theatre\\n\\nCountry of Origin: UK\\n\\nRuntime: 92 mins\\n\\n\\n\\n_________________________________\\n\\n\\n\\n4pm - Foreign Shorts 1\\n\\nBag People (Valentin Classen) - France\\n\\nHide (Brendan Hubbard) USA\\n\\nForever, Liam (Guillermo de la Rosa) - Canada/Venezuela\\n\\nRoots (Konstantinos Doxiadis) - Greece\\n\\nMade from Leakproof Plastic (Anastasiya Mykhaylova) - Canada\\n\\n__________________________________\\n\\n\\n\\n6.15pm - Feature\\n\\nTitle: Invincible\\nDirector: Emma Croft\\nVenue: Hen & Chickens Theatre\\nCountry of Origin: UK\\nRuntime: 109 mins\\nSet in June 2012, against the backdrop of the recession and the Afghanistan conflict, Emily and Oliver leave behind their comfortable middle-class life in London to start anew in a small northern town in England. Emily is eager to immerse herself in the lives of what she calls \\\"real people,\\\" while Oliver seeks relief from mounting financial pressure.\\n\\nTo foster a sense of community, Emily invites their new neighbours Alan and Dawn over for a gathering. However, what begins as an attempt at connection quickly spirals into a clash of ideologies, particularly around art, war and culture. The evening culminates in a shocking revelation that sets the stage for unforeseen consequences.\\n\\nAs tensions rise, the lives of these four neighbours begin to unravel. Emily's idealistic pursuit of solidarity falters, Oliver's increasingly dubious behavior creates fractures, and the mysterious disappearance of Alan’s cat adds to the growing chaos. Meanwhile, Emily faces a relapse into old habits, oblivious to the dramatic shift unfolding around her.\\n\\nBy the story's end, a tragedy shatters the fragile balance: Dawn and Alan’s marriage is on the brink of collapse, with Dawn spiraling into mental distress after a devastating loss. Amid the turmoil, Oliver is determined to move his family back to London, seeking escape from the mess and turmoil they have unwittingly created.\\n\\n\\n\\n__________________________________\\n\\n\\n\\n8.30pm - Feature\\nTitle: A Teachers Gift\\nDirector: Artur Ribeiro\\nVenue: Hen & Chickens Theatre\\nCountry of Origin: UK\\nRuntime: 104 mins\\n\\nRohan’s diploma may be fake but he’s a great Hindi language teacher with a knack for engaging with his retired English students and enjoying life despite his troubled past. He isn’t getting any younger and his mother is relentless in pressuring him to marry Mumbai based entrepreneur Arushi who is already in a relationship but is equally under pressure from her Father to marry Rohan.\\n\\nEnter Charles, a charming, sophisticated older Englishman with a lifestyle Rohan has only dreamt of who now enrols in his class. A relationship develops as they enjoy their common interests in literature, cricket and each other’s company despite their cultural and age differences. A sudden phone call about Arushi’s imminent arrival in London panics Rohan and he seeks immediate help from his new friend Charles. Charles agrees but for a price. A trip to India to help him with \\\"unfinished business\\\".\\n\\nAs Rohan accompanies Charles to India tensions rise between Arushi and Rohan. Matters only get worse when Charles goes missing and suspicion of murder falls on Rohan. This dramatic and frightening event in Goa eventually forces Charles, Rohan and Arushi to come clean, confront their own past, complete the unfinished business and for once in their lives face up to the truth.\\n\",\"price\":10.00,\"image_url\":\"https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/tickets.okedia.com/event_cover/day-4-hc-GMhhz.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-04-06T10:09:37.51094+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-21T12:48:53.394613+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":null,\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"168\",\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-film-festival-2026-day-4-hen-chickens-theatre\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"4e88d429-5727-4653-a1f6-3e4467289f7b\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Film Festival 2026: Day 2 (Hen & Chickens Theatre)\",\"description\":\"28th April 3 pm £10\\n\\nTitle: About My Mom\\nDirector: Soner Sert\\nVenue: Hen & Chickens Theatre\\nCountry of Origin: Turkey\\n\\nRuntime: 94 minutes\\n\\nCaner, who went to Germany to study at university, returns to Türkiye to attend the fifth anniversary commemoration of his mother's death, and is greeted at the airport by his father Muharrem, whom he has not seen for a long time. Caner, who is going to set off on a long journey to the countryside of Türkiye to attend the commemoration where all the relatives will gather and perform religious rituals with his father, whom he sees as responsible for his mother's death, enters into a fierce struggle with his father on this journey. In this journey, where the sociopolitical environment of the country forms the background, things will get even more complicated when Caner's mother gets involved between the father and son on a dark night. A modern Oedipus Complex story...\",\"price\":10.00,\"image_url\":\"https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/tickets.okedia.com/event_cover/screenshot-2026-03-21-at-162728-AQmsv.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-04-06T10:09:37.351882+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-06T12:41:01.989681+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":null,\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"165\",\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-film-festival-2026-day-2-hen-chickens-theatre\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"3a11d219-3348-44ea-8388-10ed45810528\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: Full Festival Pass\",\"description\":\"27th October - 1st November.\\nA pass to all screenings and events at UVHFF 2026 (apart from the opening night gala on 26th)\",\"price\":40.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790677344281_b1hQAaVHH.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-29T10:22:27.946914+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-29T10:24:26.728126+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abb9163ead997d09a6bb6ca\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":null,\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-full-festival-pass\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"39b35fdb-d3dd-4c2d-beb4-1137bd77d940\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Film Festival 2026: Day 3 (Hen & Chickens Theatre)\",\"description\":\"29th April £10 per screening, £15 Day Pass.\\n\\n1:45pm - Feature Film\\nTitle: Small Gods\\nDirector: Asher Rosen\\nVenue: Hen & Chickens Theatre\\nCountry of Origin: Uganda\\nRuntime: 107 mins\\n\\nWhile struggling to provide for her son, an indigenous single mother falls for a charismatic street performer. But when a crisis strikes, it threatens to rip their nascent family apart…\\n\\n____________________________________\\n\\n4 pm - Foreign Short Films\\n\\nThe Secret Assistants (Katey Lee Carson) - France/Germany/UK\\nOur Little Act of Rebellion (Ranw Aso-Rashid) - Greece\\nThe Trophy King (Tighe Boudreaux Kellner) - USA\\nAn Excess Baggage (Myriam Garcia Marienstras) - France\\nLancastria (Joséphine DURAND, Noa VALADOUX, Loris ECK, Thomas ACCORSI, William ARIZA, Garance MICOL) - France\\nNani (Mainak Dhar) - USA\\nThe Conversation Has Been Removed (Andrew Nolan) - Ireland\\n\\n__________________________________\\n\\n6 pm - Documentaries\\n\\nThe Dying Trade (Jack Hancock-Fairs) - UK\\nEsme Boggart (Nicholas Jones) - UK\\n\\n__________________________________\\n\\n8 pm - Feature Film\\n\\nTitle: Breakwater\\nDirector: Max Morgan\\nVenue: Hen & Chickens Theatre\\nCountry of Origin: UK\\nRuntime: 91 mins\\n\\nBreakwater follows the tentative romance between university student Otto and retired angler John.\",\"price\":10.00,\"image_url\":\"https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/tickets.okedia.com/event_cover/day-3-hc-6PTG9.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-04-06T10:09:37.472047+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-06T12:46:43.163044+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":null,\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"167\",\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-film-festival-2026-day-3-hen-chickens-theatre\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"26fee51e-b89d-41c2-8ca3-ae2d02f59283\",\"title\":\"Accessible online screening of...  UVFF 2026: The Black Box: Awaken\",\"description\":\"28th April - 3rd May £5\\n\\nAn accessible version of The BlackBox:  Awaken\\n\\nDirected By Rebecca Holbourn\\n\\nWritten and starring: Thom Jackson-Wood\\n\\nA young man with the chronic illness Myalgic Encephalomyelitis struggles to move forward in life because of his condition, trapping him inside a black box.\\n\\nWatching link will be supplied at checkout.\\n\\nALL PROCEEDS FROM THIS ONLINE SCREENING WILL GO TO THE FILMMAKERS TO SUPPORT THEIR NEXT PROJECT.\",\"price\":0.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1777376891669_7zcjynJtN.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-04-28T11:48:14.072412+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-28T13:17:38.135703+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"69f09e7d5c7cd75eb810b355\",\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":null,\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"189\",\"slug\":\"accessible-online-screening-of-uvff-2026-the-black-box-awaken\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"dc78646c-a885-4642-b39c-2dc101c44719\",\"title\":\"Protest & Recognition In Queer Islington: Film | Framed & Reframed Youth\",\"description\":\"18th June 6.30pm £FREE\\nReseve Seats HERE: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/protest-recognition-in-queer-islington-film-framed-reframed-youth-tickets-1990575130801?aff=oddtdtcreator\\n\\nVital LGBTQIA+ films screened, plus live discussion, to mark Pride Month at Your Story Festival\\nFramed Youth: The Revenge of the Teenage Perverts (1983) and Reframed Youth (2013)\\nwith live discussion panel: Ed Webb-Ingall, Nazmia Jamal, and Jesse Ashman.\\nFor audiences 18+. Please arrive for Doors at 6pm. Films begin at 6.30pm\\nDon't forget to view the Protest & Recognition In Queer Islington art exhibit at Union Chapel, including a celebration event with special guests on Saturday 27 June.\\nPart of Your Story Festival | 18 June - 19 September 2026\\nPart of Sunday School Stories Project\",\"price\":0.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1780396159112_gY2sRXADV.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-06-02T10:21:14.395382+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-06-18T14:27:57.350847+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6a1eb0805c7cd75eb8f6cf84\",\"age_rating\":\"16+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"protest-recognition-in-queer-islington-film-framed-reframed-youth\",\"on_sale_date\":\"2026-06-01T23:00:00+00:00\",\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/protest-recognition-in-queer-islington-film-framed-reframed-youth-tickets-1990575130801?aff=oddtdtcreator\"}, \n {\"id\":\"8e67d70c-cff6-435a-86da-428cdb0d8583\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Film Festival 2026: Day 5 (Hen & Chickens Theatre)\",\"description\":\"1st May £10 -£12 per screening, £20 for a day pass\\n\\n**12 pm - Documentaries 2**\\n**The Banjo Boys** (Johan Nayar)\\n**Houdini II: A Beautiful Day to Die**(Daniel John)\\n\\n_________________________________\\n\\n**2 pm - Documentaries 3**\\n**When You Were Young Were You Afraid of The Moon?** (Phoebe Cottam)\\n**Voice Shift** (Roberto Duque)\\n**Seekers** (Gio Israel)\\n\\n________________________________\\n\\n3.30 pm - Unrestricted Brew\\nA chance to meet and chat about the films and filmmaking. Which will lead on to...\\n\\nSpeed questions hosted by Felicity Wren (Vice President of The International Screenwriters Association)\\n\\n4pm – Speed questions 1 with: Josic Cadoret (Film London & BFI Network)\\nhttps://filmlondon.org.uk\\n\\n5 pm - Speed questions 1 with: Christine Hartland (Co founder and COO of My Smash Media)\\nhttps://www.mysmash.media\\n\\n6pm  Speed questions 2 with: Christian Parton (founder & CEO of Genera Films)\\nhttps://generafilms.com\\n\\n7pm - Speed questions 3 with: Barry Ryan (CEO of Free at Last TV & The Format Factory)\\nhttps://www.freeatlasttv.co.uk\\n\\nA 30-minute opportunity to ask an industry expert any question you like and get advice on your next project.\\n\\n_________________________________________\\n\\n**8.30 pm - Featurettes**\\n\\nMargate Barred (Ben Cole)\\n\\nWhere You At? (Shanti Scalpello)\",\"price\":10.00,\"image_url\":\"https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/tickets.okedia.com/event_cover/screenshot-2026-03-22-at-133051-jtntt.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-04-06T10:09:37.546181+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-23T17:33:09.639549+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":null,\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"170\",\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-film-festival-2026-day-5-hen-chickens-theatre\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"c2f70f9a-772a-42d0-9143-a7e603186fd9\",\"title\":\"London Fetish film Festival: A Body To Live In\",\"description\":\"5th June 7.30pm £10\\n\\n\\n\\nA BODY TO LIVE IN\\n\\nFriday June 5th, 7:30pm\\n\\nRun time 98mins\\n\\nTickets £10\\n\\nThe London Fetish Film Festival returns to its original birthplace for our second exclusive pop-up event of 2026.\\n\\nAfter selling out and generating huge demand during our February 2026 programme, we are honoured to present a second exclusive screening of Angelo Madsen’s powerful feature documentary A BODY TO LIVE IN...\\n\\n\\\"The queer art of Body modification took center stage in 1989 when Fakir Musafar’s “Modern Primitives” movement hit alternative cultures around the globe via the punk subcultural magazine Re/Search. A photographer, performance artist, and ritualist, Musafar’s work mobilized an entire generation of artists, thinkers, and seekers. A Body To Live In introduces this riveting “Gender Flex” icon to uncover the rich history of western body modification and its complex intersection with sexuality and spiritual practices.\\\"\\n\\nCREDITS:\\n\\nWriter/Director/Editor: Angelo Madsen (Previously known as Madsen Minax)\\n\\nProducers: Angelo Madsen, Lyle Ravi Kash\\nAssociate Producer: Luka Fisher\\n\\nDirector of Photography: Talena Sanders\\n\\nEP/Production: Cinereach & HARD FLOW\\nAdditional: Guggenheim Foundation, Catapult Film Fund, LEF Foundation, Vermont Arts Council, Sundance Film Institute\\n\\nFEATURING:\\n\\nFakir Musafar\\n\\nCléo Dubois \\n\\nRon Athey\\n\\nAnnie Sprinkle\\n\\nMidori\\n\\nYossie Silverman\\n\\nGanymede Cupbearer\\nV.Vale\\n\\nPaul King\\n\\nRig Daddy\\n\\nSam Winslow\\n\\n\\n\\nABOUT LFFF:\\n\\nLondon Fetish Film Festival is an international platform unleashing fearless cinema that dives into kink, fetish, BDSM, psychology, desire and power with hardcore substance, and zero shame. From arthouse to explicit, tender to transgressive, we celebrate films that smash taboos, challenge censorship, and electrify audiences through bold, provocative, and deeply human explorations of fetish culture and lifestyle.\\n\\nWe are currently accepting film submissions for LFFF 2027 here: London Fetish Film Festival - FilmFreeway\\n\\nFor the latest updates and information:  https://www.instagram.com/londonfetishfilmfestival_\",\"price\":0.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1779616188280_zi2j7UTls.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-05-23T09:28:35.980779+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-05-24T09:49:49.564458+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6a12c9bd5c7cd75eb8bf048e\",\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"204\",\"slug\":\"london-fetish-film-festival-a-body-to-live-in\",\"on_sale_date\":\"2026-05-22T23:00:00+00:00\",\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"295999c2-4d40-4086-86c6-ab36d16731d5\",\"title\":\"Protest & Recognition In Queer Islington: Film | Prick Up Your Ears\",\"description\":\"21st June 6.30pm £FREE\\n\\nReserve tickets here: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/protest-recognition-in-queer-islington-film-prick-up-your-ears-tickets-1990578955240?aff=oddtdtcreator\\n\\nVital LGBTQIA+ films screened to mark Pride Month at Your Story Festival\\nPrick Up Your Ears (1987)\\nA Cleveland Zentim film with Gary Oldman, Alfred Molina & Vanessa Redgrave. Screenplay by Alan Bennett & David Hare.\\nFor audiences 18+. Please arrive for Doors at 6pm. Films begin at 6.30pm\\nDon't forget to view the Protest & Recognition In Queer Islington art exhibit at Union Chapel, including a celebration event with special guests on Saturday 27 June.\\nPart of Your Story Festival | 18 June - 19 September 2026\\nPart of Sunday School Stories Project\\n\",\"price\":0.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1780396863574_xs4PGPYsY.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-06-02T10:41:05.90435+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-06-18T14:29:46.190125+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6a1eb3415c7cd75eb805685a\",\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"protest-recognition-in-queer-islington-film-prick-up-your-ears\",\"on_sale_date\":\"2026-06-01T23:00:00+00:00\",\"trailer_url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GpYSqJZosEU\",\"external_booking_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/protest-recognition-in-queer-islington-film-prick-up-your-ears-tickets-1990578955240?aff=oddtdtcreator\"}, \n {\"id\":\"975f7e7c-8fba-49b3-b05e-0c59ab6c6898\",\"title\":\"Protest & Recognition In Queer Islington: Selection of experimental films\",\"description\":\"28th June 6.30pm £FREE\\n\\nReserve tickets here: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/protest-recognition-in-queer-islington-selection-of-experimental-films-tickets-1990579520932?aff=oddtdtcreator\\n\\nVital LGBTQIA+ films screened, plus live discussion, to mark Pride Month at Your Story Festival\\nSelection of experimental films from artists including Roman Manfredi, Ruth Novaczek, Sarah Pucill, Alice May Williams, and Del LaGrace Volcano.\\nwith live discussion led by Cherry Smyth.\\nFor audiences 18+. Please arrive for Doors at 6pm. Films begin at 6.30pm\\nDon't forget to view the Protest & Recognition In Queer Islington art exhibit at Union Chapel, including a celebration event with special guests on Saturday 27 June.\\n\\n[Photo: Still from Tra Verso, courtesy of Roman Manfredi]\\nPart of Your Story Festival | 18 June - 19 September 2026\\nPart of Sunday School Stories Project\",\"price\":0.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1780397391974_CyAXmlJ6nf.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-06-02T10:49:54.657781+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-06-18T14:31:28.022237+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6a1eb5525c7cd75eb81103d5\",\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"protest-recognition-in-queer-islington-selection-of-experimental-films\",\"on_sale_date\":\"2026-06-01T23:00:00+00:00\",\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/protest-recognition-in-queer-islington-selection-of-experimental-films-tickets-1990579520932?aff=oddtdtcreator\"}, \n {\"id\":\"bb4b7999-f9f0-40a4-92b3-21e2a3490191\",\"title\":\"Saturn Returns Film Festival 2026\",\"description\":\"19th September 6pm & 8pm\\n\\n6PM - Short Film Block\\nCome along for our final evening and stick around for the awards.\\nFilms include: Paper Roses, Heart of a Dominatrix and La Grande Manovra.\\n\\n8PM - Short Film Block\\nCome along for our final evening and stick around for the awards.\\nFilms include: Stasis Society, Behind the Reflection, Stoop Chat and I am Autistic and Also that Bitch.\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1788439443047_gDpjvYgy1.jpeg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-03T12:44:05.353977+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-03T12:44:05.353977+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6a996b94ead997d09a2e687d\",\"age_rating\":\"16+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"saturn-returns-film-festival-2026-1\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"27667b0e-2ab3-4772-a768-b2383372c61e\",\"title\":\"UVFF Funding Lab: Blowing Up\",\"description\":\"13th September 1.30pm £10\\n\\nUVFF Fundraising Lab proudly presents,\\n\\nBlowing Up, written and directed by Faye Treacy\\n\\nStarring Gemma Fray, Rosie Holt, Phil Ellis and Frankie Boyle.\\n\\nBased on a true story\\n\\n14-year-old band geek Erin is off on tour and needs her parents to get her to the coach call on time. Yet her parents, Clive and Sandra, are distracted by their own crumbling marriage... Tensions boil over at dinner, when Sandra, determined to get a rise out of her husband invites a wildly inappropriate guest to dinner, a s3x doll called Michael (voiced by Frankie Boyle.)\\n\\nBuy a ghost ticket to attend our exclusive W.I.P screening on the 13th of September at the Hens and Chickens Theatre, London, where we will be joined by some of the cast and crew to talk about the film and the filmmaking experience to date.\\nThis is a chance to support getting the film over its last hump.\\n \\n·      Get the strings and percussion in a studio. To join the other fabulous musicians, we’ve got to record remotely. We’re all about the live musicians.\\n\\n\\n\\n·      Titles & Graphics: Design high-quality opening and closing title sequences.\\n\\n \\n\\n·      Film Festival Fees: We’ve already been accepted to some festivals (very exciting) so we’d like to submit to some more prominent festivals for wider exposure.\\n \\n·      Translation & Subtitling: Reach a broader audience with subtitles for international markets.\\n\\nThis is a chance to support getting the film over its last hump.\\n\\nOr alternately please support our campaign via crowdfunder.\\nhttps://www.crowdfunder.co.uk/p/blowing-up\",\"price\":0.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1785410219137_q_Q9yJty4.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-07-30T11:17:04.024452+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-30T11:17:04.024452+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6a6b32af5c7cd75eb86546da\",\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":null,\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"225\",\"slug\":\"uvff-funding-lab-blowing-up\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"4208b94b-eaea-4e10-ae16-5e277f181302\",\"title\":\"Saturn Returns Film Festival 2026\",\"description\":\"17th September 6pm & 8pm £12 (per screening).\\n\\n6PM - Short Film Block\\nFilms include: This is our festival launch evening, The first block starts at 6pm. Films include: Contraceptive Fair, Midnight Murungai, Trust to Trauma, Kitty, Lone, The Wake Up. \\n\\n8PM - Short Film Block\\n8pm Films include: Beached, Terradread, Women on the Fringe, She makes a Moving Picture, Sister Anna, Bruised Fruit, Muddled Meals.\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1788439125186_m5NE_XHV-.jpeg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-03T12:38:46.858514+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-03T12:38:46.858514+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6a996a56ead997d09a1cf20d\",\"age_rating\":\"16+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"saturn-returns-film-festival-2026\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"6f76113c-d74f-48e3-b5b6-281e767d6f00\",\"title\":\"UVFF Funding Lab: CELEBRATING TCHAIKOVSKY \",\"description\":\"18th October 1.30pm £10/PWYC\\nJoin us for the UVFF Film Lab Premiere of CELEBRATING TCHAIKOVSKY, a comedy short film, followed by a Q&A with the filmmakers & cast.\\n\\nWhen an impatient driver’s ambition threatens her sanity, two cheeky refuse collectors help her see sense.\\n\\nMade by Well Made Films and Dumb Blonde Productions in association with Iron Box Films, with full post-sound production sponsorship from ThinkSpace, the film was directed by Mariam Majid (Like Buses), produced by Annie Lees-Jones (Two Minutes), Will Nash (Dead Gigolo), and stars Eliza Williams (Doctors, About a Boy) alongside Mark Saramas and Matt Crosby (Coronation Street).\\n\\nSunday 18th October 2026\\nHens & Chickens Theatre, London\\nDoors from 1:00pm \\nScreening 1:30pm \\nQ&A to follow\\nGuests are warmly invited to join us for drinks following the screening.\\n\\n\\nLine-up includes Q&A with producers Annie Lees-Jones and Will Nash, director Mariam Majid and writer Louise Monaghan, Composer Ella Lindforth DeLaney as well as guest cast appearances from Eliza Williams, Mark Saramas and Matt Crosby\\n\\n\\nAgenda\\n01:00 PM - 01:30 PM\\nRed Carpet, Photography & Arrivals\\n\\nJoin us at Hens & Chickens Theatre for arrivals, red carpet photography and drinks ahead of the screening.\\n01:30PM - 02:00PM\\nCELEBRATING TCHAIKOVSKY Screening followed by Cast & Filmmaker Q&A\\n\\nJoin the cast, filmmakers and guests for the premiere. We'd love to continue the evening together and celebrate CELEBRATING TCHAIKOVSKY London Premiere.\",\"price\":0.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1789402179161_ZjzMeKsjG.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-14T16:09:41.405221+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-14T16:09:41.405221+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6aa81c44ead997d09a9a1952\",\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":true,\"legacy_widget_html\":\"226\",\"slug\":\"uvff-funding-lab-celebrating-tchaikovsky\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"4a04fdf2-b099-4604-89b7-6e02fb2d5e13\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: Blockhead\",\"description\":\"29th October 7.30pm £12\\n\\nDirected by Matt Harlock\\nUK\\n81 mins\\n\\nA failing novelist thinks his muse appears to inspire him. Instead his life spirals into chaos and murder - but just possibly, genius.\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790760903488_Z8gGYDETZ.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T09:35:07.380694+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-30T09:35:07.380694+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abcd7caead997d09a30cbdb\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-blockhead\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ipr1CLADgwM\",\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"ad592ac2-e4e1-41e4-be76-53a112be9032\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: The Rocky Horror Picture Show\",\"description\":\"31st October 9pm £12\\n\\nJoin us for this classic Comedy/musical/horror. With pizza and prosecco!\\n\\nFancy dress optional\\nPyjamas optional (we'll be wearing ours!!)\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790764221216_Ezawe9BOQ.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T10:30:23.640281+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-30T10:30:23.640281+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abce4beead997d09a7ef99b\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-the-rocky-horror-picture-show\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4plqh6obZW4\",\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"1c056613-d0f1-4652-81fc-c16c6c44fca9\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: DAY PASS - 29th October\",\"description\":\"29th October \\n\\nA day pass to see 3 fantastic Independent feature films\\n\\n3.30pm Hidden in the dark\\tChristian Gatto\\tBulgaria\\n\\t\\t\\t\\n5.30pm - Á Huldu - The Hidden Ones\\t(Darren Borrowman\\tCanada/Iceland)\\n\\t\\t\\n7.30pm - Blockhead\\t(Matt Harlock\\tUK)\",\"price\":20.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790767640587_Zsf1LPQBW.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T11:27:26.887433+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-30T11:27:26.887433+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abcf21eead997d09ad35901\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-day-pass-29th-october\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"d1e71d74-4b6e-44c6-86e9-a7ec9f22f4d4\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: Final Horror Shorts - SHORTS 6\",\"description\":\"1st November 2.30pm £12\\n\\nWe finish the festival screening as we started it, with a selection of fantastic horror short films!\\n\\nVetala\\t(Ajit Mann\\tUK)\\nEntry 8 \\t(Alastaire Bird, Megan O'Loughlin\\tUK)\\nThe Beast \\t(Yana Alzhanova\\tKazakhstan)\\nGeist \\t(William B. James\\tGermany)\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790765611594_bRWPZNhK8.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T10:52:44.563907+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-01T12:39:07.591182+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abcea2dead997d09aa8bdb2\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-final-horror-shorts\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"4e9f6775-021b-4874-aeb7-72ae5079bece\",\"title\":\"UNRESTRICTED VIEW HORROR FILM FESTIVAL 2026 X BIFA: SAINT MAUD\",\"description\":\"1st November 12.30pm £12\\n\\nDirected by Rose Glass\\nUK\\n85 mins\\n\\nIn collaboration with our friends at BIFA we are screen ing the brilliant award winning SAINT MAUD.\\nThe debut feature from Rose Glass follows a devout live-in nurse, Maud, who becomes enraptured with her new patient, the glamorous ex-dancer Amanda. Maud’s fixation soon mutates into an obsessive mission to save Amanda’s soul.\\n\\nBIFA 2020 Winner - The Douglas Hickox Award (Best Debut Director) Rose Glass BIFA 2020 Winner - Best Cinematography - Ben Fordesman  \",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1791474217083_vConk2hUb.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T10:44:12.114441+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-08T15:43:39.519398+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6ac7ba2bead997d09ab05cfe\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-saint-maud-bifa-screening\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EXs2-TY9qok\",\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"ae6ffab7-9c85-47db-80be-69dd416ff2f6\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: 27th Oct - Odeon Luxe & Dine (Screen 1) - SHORTS 2\",\"description\":\"27th October 6pm £12\\n\\nOur second night takes us to the fantastic Odeon Luxe & Dine Islington for a selection of excellent short films.\\n\\nThe Eating Of Sin (Gaius Milne Brown\\tUK)\\nSundowning (Aimie Willemse\\tUK)\\nWarren Mann: The Dark Room\\t(Dylan Hayes\\tUK)\\nBloodsuckers (Rosie Brear\\tUK)\\nAutopilot (Desi Ivanova\\tUK)\\nDraman\\t(Lazio Zana\\tIraq)\\nWrap it up\\t(Zak Harney\\tUK)\\nThe Cleanse\\t(Tim Auld\\tUK)\\nThe Man That I Wave At \\t(Ben S Hyland\\tUK)\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790681239058_zYw1o3eT3.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-29T09:52:41.407336+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-01T12:37:16.578062+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abba099ead997d09acb5780\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"797893a8-e6f4-4f29-a91e-2dd6f187ad77\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-27th-oct-odeon-luxe-dine-screen-1\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"6e3508ca-0b2c-4e0c-90d3-ce4fb7129c3c\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: The Silence of The Lambs\",\"description\":\"31st October 6.30pm £12\\n\\nJoin us for this classic horror. With pizza and prosecco!\\n\\nFancy dress optional\\nPyjamas optional (we'll be wearing ours!!)\\n\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790763826415_4ZV4nyzzi.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T10:23:49.252527+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-30T10:23:49.252527+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abce334ead997d09a785dd2\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-the-silence-of-the-lambs\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6iB21hsprAQ\",\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"20c42938-7466-447d-b325-c906bd476ea4\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: 27th Oct - Odeon Luxe & Dine (Screen 5) - SHORTS 3\",\"description\":\"27th October 6pm £12\\n\\nOur second night takes us to the fantastic Odeon Luxe & Dine Islington for a selection of excellent short films.\\n\\nThe Higher Path (Duncan Roe\\tUK)\\nCrèche & Burn (Frank O'Neil\\tUK)\\nPiping Hot Throughout (Richard Jackson\\tUK)\\nOl' Silus (Phillip Ashley Trow\\tUK)\\n3:03am (Kolya Denton\\tUK)\\nOz (Bétina Flender France)\\nChimera (Eamonn Hearns UK)\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790682972775_2YTYf6PO2H.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-29T09:56:25.752212+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-01T12:37:40.563787+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abba75eead997d09afe6f8b\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"797893a8-e6f4-4f29-a91e-2dd6f187ad77\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-27th-oct-odeon-luxe-dine-screen-5\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"0e076e8f-c7ce-4fa1-bdec-2e6c299fb199\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: 28th Oct - Arthouse Crouch End - SHORTS 4\",\"description\":\"28th October 7.30pm £12\\n\\nOur Third night takes us to the beautiful ArtHouse Crouch End for a selection of excellent short films.\\n\\nAfter Glow\\t(Aaran McKenzie\\tUK)\\nWhat Goes Round (Or Things That Go Bump In The Night) (Edie Deffebach\\tUK)\\nClean\\t(Ed McCulloch\\tUK)\\nCyclops\\t(Tariq Sayed\\tUK)\\nThe Suicide Shift\\t(Paul Laight\\tUK)\\nNo One is Coming to Rescue You (Ruth Platt\\tUK)\\nGripper\\t(Krishna Muthurangu\\tUK)\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790683777482_fm6UJoTTV.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-29T10:00:53.744929+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-01T12:38:08.524752+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abbaa83ead997d09a10f927\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"6173c46d-59a4-4316-8a59-b233557e81f6\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-28th-oct-arthouse-crouch-end\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"bcbc2048-407b-43c7-8246-fdcdfd3b97bd\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film festival 2026: Á Huldu - The Hidden Ones\",\"description\":\"29th October 5.30pm £12\\nDirected by Darren Borrowman\\nCanada/Iceland\\n85 mins\\n\\nIn the Icelandic countryside, a news cameraman is found dead under unsettling circumstances.\\nHis reporter colleague has vanished without a trace.\\nThe mystery remains unsolved.\\nYears later, a documentary crew retraces the investigation, piecing together fragments of testimony, archival material, and newly uncovered footage.\\nWhat begins as a cold case review becomes something more elusive as new evidence reveals hidden connections and unanswered questions.\\n\\nÁ Huldu – The Hidden Ones is an 85-minute English and Icelandic-language feature that adopts a true-crime documentary framework to explore the instability of truth, the ethics of observation, and the persistence of unresolved narratives.\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790759988506_g96E1-emB.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T09:19:50.771892+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-30T09:30:59.636336+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abcd436ead997d09a21080f\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-huldu-the-hidden-ones\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bCj-2LnQsEc\",\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"235812d8-cdef-4b75-a4bb-3e380087deaa\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: Hidden in the Dark\",\"description\":\"29th October 3.30pm £12\\n\\nDirected by Christian Gatto\\nBulgaria\\n100 mins\\n\\nA young girl, Maya, has been confined to a remote hospital in the mountains of Slovakia. She possesses abilities that could be a powerful advantage, but they also consume her, both physically and emotionally. Gabriel, a psychiatrist at the facility, begins to question the true purpose of the experiments conducted on her. Convinced they have little to do with a cure, he helps Maya escape, and together they take refuge in an old house. Thanks to her powers, Maya begins to perceive the presence of a little girl who seems to linger within the house, making their stay challenging, while Gabriel's good intentions also begin to become questionable.\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790760517110_9D8xYFYjP.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T09:28:39.312902+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-30T09:37:15.910144+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abcd646ead997d09a2a598c\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"hidden-in-the-dark\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c6YDcyY6RL8\",\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"a7de6e70-c40a-4369-9d0f-191768b50c1f\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: The Death Of Us \",\"description\":\"30th October 1pm £12\\n\\nDirected by Annabella Richinda Rich\\nUK\\n88 mins\\n\\nAfter the brutal loss of their child, a grieving couple retreats to the countryside, where a malevolent entity twists their reality into a waking nightmare.\\n\\nA renowned author and his wife seek refuge in the countryside after a devastating tragedy - the loss of their child in a brutal home invasion. As their grief consumes them, they soon realise memories are far from the only things haunting them. Struggling to heal, a malevolent entity emerges, twisting their reality and pulling them into an insidious plot that threatens to consume them entirely.\\n\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790761964645_a4F8ZxQiw0.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T09:52:47.924347+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-30T09:52:47.924347+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abcdbefead997d09a544cf1\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-the-death-of-us\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PaEtiPju8rI&t=1s\",\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"4fd88a4a-fdb8-461b-a789-000858e88d1a\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: Variations on Violence\",\"description\":\"30th October 3pm £12\\n\\nDirected by Zachary Nichols\\nUSA\\n71 mins\\n\\nConsumed by the distant violence he witnesses daily, a military drone pilot drifts toward self-destruction, leaving his sister to face the intimate cost of war fought far away.\\n\\nDrawn from the experiences of real U.S. military drone pilots living with PTSD, Variations on Violence visualizes trauma’s inescapable spread.\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790762437654_ELA8PIehm.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T10:00:40.043066+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-30T10:00:40.043066+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abcddc7ead997d09a5d8589\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-variations-on-violence\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"f8cd3c83-7bdc-4b9c-a664-0cf321259e86\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror film Festival 2026: Dead Reset\",\"description\":\"30th October 7pm £12\\n\\nDirected by Stewart Sparke\\nUK\\n95 mins\\n\\nTrapped in an underwater research facility, surgeon Cole Mason is forced to operate on a mutating, parasitic creature. The catch? He’s trapped in a brutal, blood-soaked time loop and must relive his own violent demise over and over again. To survive, Cole must embrace death and find a way to kill the creature and stop the loop before he becomes trapped in a never ending spiral of horror.\\n\\nBased on the video game of the same name, Dead Reset is a practical effects driven gore fest that delivers a fresh twist on the time-loop genre.\",\"price\":12.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790763367458_c0RFoQikY.png\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T10:16:09.800107+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-13T11:07:16.374719+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abce169ead997d09a703b2f\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-dead-reset\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iJiiPcmPWes&t=1s\",\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"05ee20ff-fb8c-4797-8068-03a18ccb76c8\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: DAY PASS - 30th October\",\"description\":\"30th October £20\\n\\nA day to pass to see each of the following screenings:\\n\\n1pm\\t- The Death Of Us \\t(Annabella Richinda Rich\\tUK 88 mins)\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n3pm - \\tVariations on Violence\\t(Zachary Nichols\\tUS\\t71 mins)\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n5pm -\\tWorld Shorts\\t\\t\\nExuvia\\t(Arthur Henning\\tAustria0\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\nDon't Go\\tT(alon Darren Winsnes\\tNorway)\\t\\nIn Case of Fear\\t(Aaron Sauerland\\tUSA\\t)\\nScroll\\t(Utku Banci\\tCanada)\\t\\nFavela Amarela\\t(Nícolas Lobato, Thiago Tuchu\\tBrazil)\\nThe Binding\\t(Ryan Kennedy\\tUSA)\\t\\nGumboro\\t(Dimitris Vavatsis\\tGreece)\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n7pm\\t- Dead Reset\\t(Stewart Sparke\\tUK\\t95 mins)\\n\\n\",\"price\":20.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790768261643_pHJrIsyAJ.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-30T11:37:43.994998+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-30T11:37:43.994998+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abcf487ead997d09ade95b5\",\"age_rating\":\"18+\",\"venue_id\":\"8517cff2-0b3b-4fc6-8f52-231bb610c905\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":5,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-day-pass-30th-october\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":null}, \n {\"id\":\"c641adc2-16aa-43ce-ab86-956c2aad59f1\",\"title\":\"Unrestricted View Horror Film Festival 2026: Screen on the Green - Opening Night Gala\",\"description\":\"26th October 8pm (Door at 7.30pm) \\n\\nWe launch our 2026 Horror Film Festival with a selection of fantastic UK shorts at the iconic Everyman Screen on the Green.\\n\\nAfter Birth \\t(Amy Cudden\\tUK)\\nGrandma is Thirsty \\t(Kris Carr\\tUK)\\nThe Humbug \\t(Cole Paviour\\tUK)\\nForeign Bodies\\t(Lysander Wong\\tUK/Hong Kong)\\nHomonym \\t(Lily Howkins\\tUK)\\nDissonance \\t(Edward Zorab\\tUK)\\nA Hand to Hold \\t(Philip Clyde-Smith\\tUK)\",\"price\":0.00,\"image_url\":\"https://ik.imagekit.io/3cqohyklk/events/event-1790764391013_JajebxQfc.jpg\",\"genres\":[\"Film Festival\"],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-29T09:45:04.132724+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-05T07:41:57.162413+00:00\",\"imagekit_file_id\":\"6abce568ead997d09a821769\",\"age_rating\":null,\"venue_id\":\"e241d1b7-66b9-4f7a-b9dd-a1765c16a6bc\",\"producer_id\":null,\"status\":\"published\",\"additional_booking_fee_percent\":0,\"is_legacy\":false,\"legacy_widget_html\":null,\"slug\":\"unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-opening-night-gala\",\"on_sale_date\":null,\"trailer_url\":null,\"external_booking_url\":\"https://www.everymancinema.com/film-listing/1000053024-unrestricted-view-horror-film-festival-2026-opening-night/?date=2026-10-26\"}]",
